  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Thursday)\nIssued at 1209 PM CDT FRI OCT 30 2026\n\nWater vapor imagery early this afternoon reveals a shortwave\nlifting across Texas. A plume of deep moisture associated with\nthe remnants of Tropical Storm Vance accompanying this upper\nlevel feature will combine with a swath of healthy PWATs coming\nin off the Gulf, promoting increased rain chances over the\nweekend. While the greatest chances look to come overnight, we\nwill carry low chances (20-30%) Saturday afternoon so keep that\nin mind before heading out for some trick-or-treating. With that\nsaid, some of the higher resolution guidance continues back off\nin coverage. Otherwise, the shortwave is expected to slowly lift\nnortheastward through the day on Sunday, leaving low  to medium\nchances for rain through Sunday evening.\n\nWeak ridging early next week will lead to a few rain-free days\nbefore our next system arrives by mid week. There are several\ndetails we will need to work out over the coming days such as how\nfar south the upper level low moves and how quickly it tracks\nthrough the region. For now, we will carry a moderate (40-60%)\nchance of showers and storms as ample moisture will be in place\nahead of this system.\n\n95/Castillo",
